First, identify the triangle with points M, N, P as a regular triangle with two sides of length 4 and 8. Using the Pythagorean theorem, find the length of the hypotenuse:
\begin{equation}
MN^2 + PQ^2 = MP^2
\end{equation}
\begin{align*}
MN^2 &= (4)^2 = 16 \\
PQ^2 &= (8)^2 = 64 \\
MP^2 &= (16+64)/2 = 36
\end{align*}
\begin{equation}
MP^2 - MN^2 - PQ^2 = 0 \Rightarrow MP = \sqrt{36 - 16 - 64} = 4\sqrt{3}
\end{equation}

Next, determine the height of the prism QPCDMN:
\begin{equation}
h = CD = CQ + QM = 8 + 4\sqrt{3}
\end{equation}

Finally, since the base of the prism is an equilateral triangle with side length 12, its area is:
\begin{equation}
A_{base} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4}(12)^2
\end{equation}

The volume of the prism QPCDMN is given by the formula for the volume of a prism:
\begin{equation}
V = A_{base} \times h = \frac{36\sqrt{3}}{4} \times (8+4\sqrt{3})
\end{equation}
